---
const facts = [
  { label: 'language', value: 'Rust', accent: '#dea584' },
  { label: 'edition', value: '2024' },
  { label: 'platform', value: 'Win32 API' },
  { label: 'framework', value: 'none' },
  { label: 'gpu', value: 'none · overlay' },
  { label: 'binary', value: '~2 MB' },
  { label: 'licensing', value: 'offline' },
  { label: 'telemetry', value: 'never' },
];
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pt-24 pb-16 sm:px-10 sm:pt-32">
  <header class="mb-12 grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-12">
    <div
      class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-ink-faint md:col-span-3"
    >
      § 05 / how it works
    </div>
    <h2
      class="font-display text-[34px] font-semibold leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.025em] text-ink sm:text-[42px] md:col-span-9"
    >
      A transparent window
      <span class="text-ink-muted">that knows when not to be there.</span>
    </h2>
  </header>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-x-12 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-12">
    {/* Prose — main column */}
    <div class="md:col-span-7">
      <p class="text-[16.5px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
        Limnia creates a fullscreen layered window that covers every monitor.
        Pixels with
        <span class="rounded bg-surface-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-pen">
          alpha = 0
        </span>
        are completely click-through, so the overlay is effectively invisible.
        Toggle draw mode and the canvas fills with a minimal alpha value to catch
        mouse input. Toggle off and it disappears again.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[16.5px] leading-[1.6] text-ink-muted">
        Pure Win32. No framework. The drawing overlay uses no GPU at all — every
        stroke is composited in a software BGRA buffer. The one exception is Pro
        screen recording, which taps Direct3D and Media Foundation for hardware
        H.264. The whole binary is smaller than this page.
      </p>
    </div>

    {/* Spec list — right column */}
    <dl
      class="space-y-3 font-mono text-[12.5px] md:col-span-5 md:border-l md:border-line md:pl-10"
    >
      {facts.map((f) => (
        <div class="grid grid-cols-[7rem_1fr] items-baseline">
          <dt class="uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-ink-faint">{f.label}</dt>
          <dd
            class="text-ink"
            style={f.accent ? `color: ${f.accent}` : ''}
          >{f.value}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
